HELP_TOPICS = {'mode_border_plate': {'title': 'Base Form: Frame (Border) vs. Plate / Inlay (Plate)', 'short': 'Switches between an open picture frame (Border) and a continuous metal/glass plate (Plate).', 'detail': '• FRAME (Border): The center remains open (transparent) to frame your photo or artwork.\n• PLATE / INLAY (Plate): The center is filled as a solid, brushed, or semi-transparent metal/glass mirror or colored inlay bed (ideal for logos, badges & nameplates).'}, 'grow_direction': {'title': 'Growth Direction (Outward, Inward, Both)', 'short': 'Controls whether the frame grows outward, inward, or centered along the selection edge.', 'detail': '• Outward (Expand image): The frame is built outside your selection. If margin space is insufficient, Borderlay automatically expands the GIMP canvas.\n• Inward: The frame grows from the selection edge toward the center.\n• Both (Centered): The frame straddles the selection edge (50% outward, 50% inward).'}, 'corner_radii': {'title': 'Corners & Radii (Outer and Inner Radius)', 'short': 'Controls the rounding of outer and inner frame corners (0 px = sharp 45° miter joint). Available from Community.', 'detail': "• Soft / Medium / Subtle (Radius > 0 px): Creates concentrically rounded corners like a stamped metal plate.\n• 45° Miter (0 / 0 px): Creates a classic frame with sharp 90° corners and true diagonal 45° miter joints.\n• In tab '2. Geometry, Radii & 3D' you can adjust outer and inner radii independently in pixels."}, 'path_toolbox': {'title': 'Path Toolbox (Atelier / Team)', 'short': 'Fits a circle, ellipse, rectangle, triangle, sine, or parabola into the current selection.', 'detail': '• The selection box is the frame. With no selection there is no path and no frame.\n• Set path writes the curve as a GIMP path and does not render a border.\n• Copies along path duplicates the selection along that path, spaced across its full length.\n• Leave the check off and each copy keeps its orientation. Turn it on and the copy follows the path direction.\n• Fading Steps and End Transparency use the same sums as the rotation series. Rotation on the axis stays the other placement.'}, 'shape_toolbox': {'title': 'Selection Shapes & Align (Look / Atelier)', 'short': 'Sets a shape as the selection and aligns it. No frame is rendered.', 'detail': '• Tap a category at the top. Each shape is a tile. Under the name is its id, for example leaf.heart. The same id sits under the large preview and can be selected.\n• Size, angle, and parameters draw the shape on the image at once, filled with a color you choose.\n• Apply removes the color and sets the selection. Close without applying removes the color and restores the previous selection.\n• Look shows basic shapes, one wave, and one smile.\n• Atelier and Team also show flames, gears, leaves, ornament, festive shapes, arches, wave parameters, the wink, and the angle.\n• A rectangular selection is the frame. The shape starts centered in it, at its own aspect. With no selection the frame is the image and the shape starts at about 60 percent of the shorter side.\n• Align pins the shape to that frame. The arrows move it by the step, including past the frame. Width scales it around its center. The shape moves, not a layer.'}, 'shape_rotation': {'title': 'Rotate Selection Shape (Angle & 9-Point Pivot Axis)', 'short': 'Rotates only the frame around the chosen pivot – the underlying image stays untouched! Single rotation from Community.', 'detail': '• Rotation Angle (-180° to +180°): Rotates the frame or plate geometry on the canvas.\n• Leaf: tip at the top, stem at the bottom. Pivot “edge bottom center” puts the stem in the middle of the rosette.\n• Pivot Axis: Defines the anchor point of rotation – e.g. Center, Corner Top-Left, or Edge Bottom-Center.\n• Important: Your photo/layer content is NOT rotated, and global studio lighting remains physically consistent!'}, 'repeat_rotation': {'title': 'Repeat Rotation & Fade Series (Look / Atelier)', 'short': 'Automatically generates a rotated series (From–to, Until angle, Repeat, Fade cycle) with progressive transparency fade-out.', 'detail': '• From–to: one path from start to end, the fade runs once.\n• Until angle: from the start to a target angle, at most one turn.\n• Repeat: the same path sits a small step aside and the fade continues, at most four times.\n• Fade cycle: the same fade starts again after each interval. Six times 60° begins at 0°, 60°, 120°, 180°, 240° and 300°.\n• No fade keeps all copies opaque. Fading Steps subtracts opacity per copy and stops at 0. End Transparency keeps every copy and fades smoothly to the end value.'}, 'inlay_color': {'title': 'Glass & Inlay Color (incl. Eyedropper & Swatches)', 'short': "Sets the intrinsic color for 'Colored Crystal Glass' as well as recessed inlay grooves and inlay plates.", 'detail': "Where does this color apply?\n1. When material 'Colored Crystal Glass' is selected, it colors the entire glass body and refraction.\n2. When 'Recessed Colored Inlay Well' is active in Plate mode, it colors the inner mirror.\n3. In the Multi-Zone Editor, it colors any zone set to material 'Inlay Color (inlay)'.\n\nTip: Click the wide color bar for the color wheel/eyedropper or click one of the 8 gemstone swatches."}, 'metal_gradient': {'title': 'Metal Gradient & Transition Width', 'short': 'Selects between the physical 7-stop alloy curve and native GIMP gradients.', 'detail': "• Internal 7-Stop Material Curve (Recommended): Computes the physical light/shadow reflection curve for each metal (Gold, Chrome, Copper, Stainless Steel).\n• GIMP Gradient: Overrides the metal lookup with a custom GIMP gradient.\n• Adjust the transition width between slopes and plateaus via 'Bevel Softness (%)'."}, 'dual_profile_cut': {'title': 'Interactive Cross-Section Cut & Transition Width', 'short': 'Shows live in cross-section where zone colors, grooves, plate opacity, and transitions act.', 'detail': "• The cross-section displays the elevation profile from the outer edge (left) to the inner zone (right).\n• On the right, it shows live whether the interior is an open image window or a plate with the chosen opacity (%).\n• The yellow bands at zone boundaries mark the active transition width ('Bevel Softness').\n• In tab 5, click directly on Z1..Zn in the plot to focus the corresponding zone row below!"}, 'light_vector': {'title': '2D Light Vector, Source Type (Beam vs. Cone) & Impact Point', 'short': 'Graphically controls light origin -> impact point, angle (°), intensity (%), and beam width / cone diameter.', 'detail': '• Drag in the 2D vector pad from the light origin (yellow dot) to the target point (arrowhead):\n  - Direction sets the incidence angle (0°–360°, default 135° = Top-Left).\n  - Arrow length controls specular intensity (%).\n• Light Cone (Cone): Spotlight source with adjustable cone diameter (%).\n• Light Beam (Beam): Linear softbox/tube light band with adjustable beam width (%).'}, 'inner_shimmer': {'title': 'Contour-Following Inner Shimmer', 'short': 'Casts a soft metallic light glow from the inner frame edge into the inner image area.', 'detail': 'The inner shimmer hugs the innermost frame contour and can automatically follow the main light source, shine Top-Left, Backlit (Bottom-Right), or All Around.'}, 'surface_finish': {'title': 'Surface Finish: Brushed, Grained, Feathered, Fur & Scales', 'short': 'Controls surface structure from Mirror and Satin through Brushed and Grained to Feathered, Fur, and Scales.', 'detail': '• Mirror: smooth, glossy surface with crisp reflection.\n• Frosted / Satin: softly diffused sheen for satin metals or frosted glass.\n• Brushed: fine directional brush lines; Granularity adjusts line fineness and Brush Angle rotates the stroke.\n• Grained: even micro-grain / cast texture without directional brush lines.\n• Feathered: layered feather barbs with Feather Size, Feather Length, Feather Density, and Direction.\n• Fur: dense directional hair strands with Hair Length, Fur Density, and Stroke Direction.\n• Scales: overlapping scale pattern with Scale Size, Scale Length, and Scale Direction.\n• Direction “Follows light” (-1): aligns Brushed, Feathered, Fur, and Scales automatically to the light angle; any fixed angle (0° = right) overrides it.'}, 'lighting_glow': {'title': 'Lighting Effects, Specular Gloss & Glow (Bloom)', 'short': 'Controls automatic studio light, specular highlights, soft luxury glow (bloom), bevel contrast, and inner shimmer.', 'detail': "• Light mode: Auto selects a fitting light direction per material (from Community). Tab '4. Light & Effects' adds the 2D Light Vector Pad (Cone or Beam) in Atelier.\n• Specular gloss: controls strength and crispness of metallic highlight edges.\n• Glow / Luxury Bloom: adds a soft luminous halo around bright highlights so metal and glass catch the light.\n• Bevel contrast & softness: control how sharply or smoothly lit and shaded 3D slopes blend.\n• Inner shimmer: casts a contour-accurate glow from the inner frame edge into the artwork (Auto, Top-Left, Backlight, or All around)."}, 'support': {'title': 'Support', 'short': 'Support is provided only for Look, Atelier, and Team.', 'detail': 'Support is provided only for Look, Atelier, and Team.\nContact: https://www.ready-4-it.com/contact'}}
